 {
  "event": 498,
  "id": "toolu_vrtx_01GV3vbY2f4cDrPgM2nsZw2T",
  "tool": "gdocs_create_document",
  "context": "main",
  "model": "claude-opus-5-5",
  "ok": true,
  "result_event": 499,
  "input": {
   "title": "ZM3D playable - brief for PlayableX",
   "bodyText": "ZM3D playable - brief for PlayableX\nZombie Match 3D (Puzzles vs Zombies). Written 1 October 2025 for the game as it is today. If we change the core game before the build, we'll go through the affected parts with you again in November.\n\nStart date\nKickoff is Monday 3 November 2025. That's the date you gave us after we asked for the pause.\n\nScenario\nWe're going with Scenario 1. Its job is retention, not cheap installs: it should filter out players who won't like the game while staying true to the core gameplay. Unlike the Domino Delights playable, the player isn't on rails. They pick whatever items they want off the board and can make several matches if they're good enough.\n\nHow a level plays\n- The board is a 3D physics pile of items. Items settle and cover each other, so digging uncovers buried matches.\n- The player drags items into a tray with 7 slots. Any 3 matching items in the tray clear, and the cleared item is fired at the zombies from the cannon (what you've been calling the rocket launcher, with its projectile). Different items have different abilities: the grenade is powerful, the couch does splash damage, the plushie is weak but funny.\n- Zombies walk in towards us.\n- Win: every zombie on screen is eliminated.\n- Lose: the zombies reach us and our HP runs out. That's the only lose state.\n- A full tray is not a loss. If all 7 slots fill without a match it counts as a blunder: the tray clears and the surviving zombies enrage, but play goes on.\n\nThe board: 8 items\nGrenade, Couch, Plushie Chick, Shuriken, Cute Axe, Gift Box, Cactus Plant, Bow.\nEvery other board item on the pack list is an extra you can swap in, using the editable board you offered. That includes Dynamite, Couch and Pillow, Plushie Bunny and everything else in the Living Room, Survival, Toys, Bathroom, Kitchen, Music Instruments and Garden sets. The hand-off list marks each board item as Default (one of the 8) or Extra.\nThe reference level we sent on 24 September used Grenade, Couch, Couch and Pillow, Plushie Bunny and Plushie Chick. The 8 above replace that set. The Bow replaces the Dynamite from our earlier list, and the Plushie Chick is the item you called the duck.\n\nZombies: 4, one animation\nParty Girl, Plumber, Magician and Football Player, with one animation: walk. All four are in the Unity package we sent on 26 September (zombies_Characters_UnityPack.zip), so you can re-rig them in Spine from there. More zombies can come later if the scope allows.\n\nBackground and cannon\nUse the background from the reference level and the cannon with its projectile. Both went to you in the first zip on 24 September.\n\nSound\n- Use: matching, success and failure sounds. They're ours and ready.\n- Music: a new track made for the ad, not the in-game track. It's being cut down to a loop and is still to come from us. Music may only start after the player's first tap, per your rule from the Domino playable.\n- Rocket and explosion sounds: still to come. The ones in the game come from a sound library and a bought pack, so we can't hand them over. We'll send our own versions.\n\nFormats (as you gave them to us)\n- 3D: .fbx (binary, not ASCII), .glb or .blend\n- 2D: .png (character parts separated for 2D animation)\n- Font: .ttf or .woff2\n- Sound: .mp3 or .wav\n\nWhat's still coming from us\nThe hand-off list covers every line of the pack, one row each: whether you already have it (Delivered), whether it's sitting in our outgoing folder ready to send (Ready), or whether it's still owed, and if so what and who on our side has it.\n"
  }
 },
